"view.progressivecalendar.help"                              = "Choose which progressive techniques to include — transits, secondary directions and/or symbolic directions — and pick the factors for each. The factors shown reflect your configuration settings; you can add or remove factors. Select the radix factors to compare against, and which kinds of events to look for: aspects and parallels (to the radix chart, and between the progressive factors themselves), conjunctions with cusps, retrograde/direct stations, out-of-bounds moments, and zero/maximum declination.\n\nSpecify the orb for aspects, parallels and cusps.\n\nThe maximum date range depends on your selection: fast-moving factors such as a transiting Moon only allow a short range, while slower techniques allow much longer ones. The note under the date range fields shows the current maximum.\n\nSettings here are seeded from your saved configuration but apply only to this calculation — they are not written back automatically. Use 'Reset to saved settings' to discard your changes.\n\nClick 'Calculate' to see the results.";

